# Access control list for the ECG prototype broker
# ================================================
#
# Referenced by mosquitto.windows.conf (acl_file acl). Without it, every
# authenticated client could publish to every topic, and the device id inside a
# topic would mean nothing: any device could file readings as any other.
#
# Topic design (no patient data anywhere in a topic - only a device id):
#   ecg/devices/<device_id>/data     device -> server   1-second ECG chunk
#   ecg/devices/<device_id>/status   device -> server   online/offline, retained
#   ecg/devices/<device_id>/event    device -> server   reconnects, overruns
#   ecg/devices/<device_id>/result   server -> device   screening verdict
#   ecg/<device_id>/reading          legacy whole-window contract (simulator)
#   ecg/<device_id>/result           legacy verdict topic

# The backend subscribes across all devices and answers each one.
user ecg-server
topic read  ecg/devices/+/data
topic read  ecg/devices/+/status
topic read  ecg/devices/+/event
topic write ecg/devices/+/result
topic read  ecg/+/reading
topic write ecg/+/result

# One device: it may publish only its own branch and read only its own verdict.
# Topics are case-sensitive: the device id is ESP32-001, matching the firmware
# DEVICE_ID and the devices table. The broker account name stays lowercase.
# A second device gets its own block; it cannot touch this one's topics.
user esp32-001
topic write ecg/devices/ESP32-001/data
topic write ecg/devices/ESP32-001/status
topic write ecg/devices/ESP32-001/event
topic read  ecg/devices/ESP32-001/result
topic write ecg/ESP32-001/reading
topic read  ecg/ESP32-001/result
